coverage
# The CDK app isn't part of either Docker image (and cdk.out lives inside
# the same repo root used as the Docker build context — without excluding
# it, CDK's own asset-staging copy would recurse into its own output
# directory). Excluding all of infra/, not just its generated output, also
# means infra-only changes don't invalidate/rebuild the app images.
infra
*.md
!README.md
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
src/test
vitest.config.mts
.env*
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
